FINDINGS Quick: #C1066 review-waits-for-ready ced52090 (Checker 2)

M1 (collector/state.mjs peerSignalled) A peer's signal clears the hold of every card in the group or partnership, whatever that card's head is, for as long as the signalled head is open. So after one signal, any later push by another member is unheld and wakes reviewers again: the card's own case. Probe on real git (d5's setup, signal on card-two): (a) card-one pushes a WIP fix after the group went READY, unheld; (b) a new card joins g1 and makes an empty WIP start push, unheld. Both wake Checker. Groups gain cards all the time, so (b) is common. This was my option 2, and the hole is mine too: the probe cannot tell "this head was READY and waited for the group" from "this head came after". Fix: option 1. When stack-ready writes the signal for a whole group or stack, it notes the current head of every member (from the queue file and the remote tips), and the probe goes back to covered(id) alone, so a later push is a new head with no signal. Tests: (a) and (b) above held; d5's two-branch case unheld.

